 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** Interpolation introduces approximation errors, particularly in regions with high gradients [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Boundaries:** The framework assumes that coarser levels adequately cover the spatial extent of finer cells [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If a cell has no covering coarser data (e.g., at domain boundaries or extreme refinement), interpolation may fail. This is not explicitly addressed in the sources.
+*   **Precision:** Interpolation introduces approximation errors, particularly when refining from very coarse to very fine levels.
+*   **Boundaries:** Interpolation at the boundaries of AMR patches must respect patch boundaries to avoid data leakage.
+*   **Degenerate Input:** If a cell is refined in one step but has no refined neighbors in the other step (e.g., isolated refinement), interpolation may fail or produce artifacts. The sources do not specify a fallback.
 
